    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d921">

                <pb facs="0966" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg954"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121 Pyk, Irena Teodozja/22: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-30T13:00:00+03:00">April 30, 1941—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 30—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>881. Department’s 595, April 28, 5 p.m.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d921-f1"/> Pyk and
                    Roszkowski left yesterday for Vladivostok where they should be able to make
                    connections with the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Chile</hi> unless the
                    train is late in arriving.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d921-f2"/> I am informing
                        Ward<anchor n="48" xml:id="d921-f3"/> of their departure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d921-f1" n="46" xml:id="d921-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f2" n="47" xml:id="d921-f2-content">
                <p>The train was due to arrive in Vladivostok on May 9, 1941, and the two passengers
                    sailed on the S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Chile</hi> of the Johnson Line on
                    May 17.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f3" n="48" xml:id="d921-f3-content">
                <p>Angus Ivan Ward, American Consul at Vladivostok.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
